<article class="env-lemma" id="0H57">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H57">Lemma <span data-tag="0H57">62.6.8</span>.</a> In the situation of Example <a href="/tag/0H4S" data-tag="0H4S">62.5.4</a> assume $S$ is locally Noetherian and $Z$ is flat over $S$ in dimensions $\geq r$. Then $[Z/X/S]_ r$ is a relative $r$-cycle on $X/S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption means that $\mathcal{O}_ Z$ is flat over $S$ in dimensions $\geq r$. Thus applying Lemma <a href="/tag/0H56" data-tag="0H56">62.6.7</a> with $\mathcal{F} = (Z \to X)_*\mathcal{O}_ Z$ we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>